BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Medium Size
CATEGORIES:Civics
DESCRIPTION:Join President Koppell for his first lecture in the American E
 xperiment series\, where he will discuss migration\, identity\, and the A
 merican nation.\nMigration has been central to the American experience fr
 om the nation’s earliest history to the present. It has shaped the countr
 y’s population\, economy\, politics\, culture\, and understanding of nati
 onal identity\, while also generating recurring debates over citizenship\
 , belonging\, borders\, assimilation\, and exclusion. This lecture examin
 es how migration\, including internal and forced migration\, has influenc
 ed the development of the United States and how Americans have defined wh
 o belongs within the national community. It considers the tensions betwee
 n the country’s long-standing identity as a nation of immigrants and its 
 equally significant history of restriction\, exclusion\, and contested me
 mbership. The discussion will explore how race\, ethnicity\, religion\, c
 lass\, and demographic change have shaped immigration policy and public a
 ttitudes\, while placing contemporary debates over borders\, citizenship\
 , birthright citizenship\, integration\, and national identity within a b
 roader historical and constitutional context. At its center is an endurin
 g question for American democracy: How should a nation shaped by migratio
 n define membership\, belonging\, and shared identity in a period of rapi
 d global and demographic change?\n\nHosted by: Campus Activities\, Civic 
 & Voter Engagement\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://mon
 tclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12650772
DTEND:20261006T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050250Z
DTSTART:20261006T183000Z
LOCATION:Presentation Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The American Experiment \;Migration\, Identity\, and the American 
 Nation
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12650772
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12650772
X-HOSTS:Civic & Voter Engagement
END:VEVENT
