BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
DESCRIPTION:\nWhat does it take to create lasting social change - and what
  can the history of LGBTQ+ activism teach us about today's battles over e
 ducation\, identity\, and civil rights?\nJoin journalist and cultural com
 mentator Tracy E. Gilchrist\, host of Holding Space with Tracy E. Gilchri
 st and former editor-in-chief of The Advocate for a lively conversation w
 ith Professor Lisa M. Stulberg\, NYU sociologist of education and author 
 of the new book How to Win a Culture War: LGBTQ+ Social Change Through Po
 p Culture.\nDrawing on Stulberg's research into LGBTQ+ social movements\,
  education\, and political change-and Gilchrist's years covering the inte
 rsections of LGBTQ+ equality\, politics\, and popular culture-the convers
 ation will explore how movements change public attitudes\, institutions\,
  and policy\; why cultural conflicts become so powerful\; and what histor
 y can teach us about navigating the culture wars of the present.\nAn enga
 ging conversation about activism\, education\, media\, politics\, and the
  possibilities for social change. This program will include audience part
 icipation and a speed round of LGBTQ+ trivia!\nThis event is free and ope
 n to the public\, but registration is requested.REGISTER HERE\n\n\nHosted
  by: College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAdditional Infor
 mation can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/128
 48950
DTEND:20261007T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050250Z
DTSTART:20261007T213000Z
GEO:40.860890;-74.200500
LOCATION:SBUS 140
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Holding Space for Queer Social Change Through Pop Culture
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12848950
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12848950
X-HOSTS:College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)
END:VEVENT
