DESCRIPTION:Looking for ways to make the most of Summer 2027 while strengt
 hening your pre-med/health journey?\nJoin the Pre-Medical Program for an 
 interactive workshop focused on finding and applying to summer enrichment
  programs\, internships\, research experiences\, clinical opportunities\,
  volunteer programs\, and more!\nWe’ll highlight opportunities such as PU
 LSE\, NERA\, Yale summer programs\, Gateway to Dentistry\, and other pre-
 health summer experiences for students interested in medicine\, dentistry
 \, PA\, PT\, nursing\, pharmacy\, optometry\, public health\, and other h
 ealth professions.\nDuring this workshop\, you will:\nDiscover summer pro
 grams and opportunities for 2027Learn where and how to search for opportu
 nitiesReview common application requirements and deadlinesGet tips for st
 rengthening your resume and applicationLearn how to stand out as an appli
 cantHear from students who have participated in summer enrichment experie
 nces\nBring your laptop or iPad! You'll have time to search for opportuni
 ties that match your interests and begin building your personal Summer 20
 27 opportunity list.  \nThis workshop is one of the required PMP programs
  that can be completed toward eligibility for the HFNJ BLS Scholars Certi
 fication Program. \n\nHosted by: Pre-Medical Program\n\nAdditional Inform
 ation can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/1276
 4527
