BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:Faculty Concert: Chris Opperman\, Composition\nDr. Chris Opper
 man wields a special array of expertise. He is a composer of wildly origi
 nal music\, a top orchestrator and arranger\, a dedicated and visionary e
 ducator\, and a trusted advisor for an incredible cross-section of the mu
 sic industry.\nSince starting his Purple Cow Records label in 1998\, Dr. 
 Opperman has released six prior albums including 2001’s Klavierstücke\, h
 is first solo piano album\, and 2010’s The Lionheart\, an orchestral rock
  album. He has also released three EP’s including 2022’s Four Improvisati
 ons which feature studio-manipulated piano works\, and two singles includ
 ing “And If You Know” featuring Robert Martin.\nWith Arnie & Eric Roth of
  AWR Music\, Dr. Opperman has worked on several national and internationa
 l orchestral and chamber music tours including Distant Worlds: music from
  FINAL FANTASY\, A New World: intimate music from FINAL FANTASY\, the FIN
 AL FANTASY VII Remake Orchestra World Tour\, The Beach Boys Holiday Vibra
 tions Orchestra Tour\, several Mannheim Steamroller Christmas tours\, and
  Undertale LIVE. Dr. Opperman’s arrangements with AWR and others have bee
 n performed by renowned and accomplished orchestras at premiere venues wh
 ich include Carnegie Hall\, the Royal Albert Hall\, the Tokyo Internation
 al Forum\, and more.\nAlong with much other music\, Opperman played piano
  on two of Steve Vai’s Grammy-nominated compositions\, “Lotus Feet” from 
 Real Illusions: Reflections and “The Attitude Song” from Sound Theories\,
  Vols. I and II\, both with the Metropole Orkest. He’s also performed wit
 h virtuoso multi-instrumentalist Mike Keneally\, Indian classical music m
 asters L. Shankar (a.k.a. Shenkar) and Zakir Hussein\, former Duran Duran
 /Missing Persons guitarist Warren Cuccurullo\, and many others.\nDr. Oppe
 rman holds a Ph. D. In Music Composition and has taught undergraduate and
  graduate level courses on music theory and composition\, popular and cla
 ssical music history\, music technology\, and the music industry.\nLearn 
 more about Chris Opperman\n\nHosted by: The College of the Arts\n\nAdditi
 onal Information can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage
 /event/12657686
DTEND:20261009T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050250Z
DTSTART:20261009T000000Z
LOCATION:Leshowitz Recital Hall\, Chapin Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Faculty Concert: Chris Opperman\, Composition
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12657686
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12657686
X-HOSTS:The College of the Arts
END:VEVENT
