BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
CATEGORIES:Civics
DESCRIPTION:American higher education evolved from an elite system trainin
 g clergy into a vital pillar of our democracy and economic progress. Whil
 e the nation's Founders recognized the essential link between education a
 nd self-governance\, contemporary universities did not initially serve th
 is broader public purpose.\nThe first dramatic shift came during the Civi
 l War\, when the Morrill Act of 1862 established land-grant universities 
 with a public mission to train citizens in building the infrastructure an
 d agricultural capacity of a developing nation. This democratic commitmen
 t expanded over the decades to include African Americans through the 1890
  Morrill Act and to train educators via normal schools\, like Montclair\,
  at the turn of the century. Following World War II\, the "Endless Fronti
 er" report permanently linked university research with national security 
 and industrial strength. This model\, combined with the GI Bill's massive
  expansion of student access and the Bayh-Dole Act's incentives for comme
 rcializing intellectual property\, established higher education as the pr
 imary engine of modern innovation.\nToday\, universities sit at the cente
 r of critical national policy\, where federal investments simultaneously 
 ensure democratic access through student aid and drive advanced economic 
 initiatives. With many questioning the value of higher education\, this l
 ecture provides analysis of the current institutional landscape set in it
 s historical context.\n\nHosted by: Campus Activities\, Civic & Voter Eng
 agement\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.camp
 uslabs.com/engage/event/12824611
DTEND:20261013T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050250Z
DTSTART:20261013T183000Z
LOCATION:Cole Hall rm. 340
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:AMERICAN HIGHER EDUCATION: FOUNDATION OF DEMOCRACY\, ENGINE OF INN
 OVATION
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12824611
