BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
CATEGORIES:Well-Being
CATEGORIES:Medium Size
CATEGORIES:Civics
CATEGORIES:Undergraduate Students
DESCRIPTION:Democracy doesn't protect itself—it depends on informed\, enga
 ged citizens.\nJoin Civic and Voter Engagement\, in collaboration with th
 e African American Caucus\, for a powerful screening of All In: The Fight
  for Democracy\, the critically acclaimed documentary that examines the h
 istory and present-day reality of voter suppression in the United States.
  Featuring voting rights advocate Stacey Abrams\, the film explores the h
 istorical barriers\, systemic inequities\, and ongoing challenges that co
 ntinue to shape access to the ballot box and influence civic participatio
 n.\nMore than a documentary\, this screening is an opportunity to deepen 
 your understanding of the democratic process\, reflect on the importance 
 of protecting voting rights\, and engage in meaningful dialogue about one
  of the most fundamental rights in our democracy.\nFollowing the screenin
 g\, participants are invited to stay for a facilitated discussion explori
 ng the themes of the film\, the significance of voting rights in today's 
 political landscape\, and the role each of us can play in strengthening o
 ur democracy through civic engagement. Whether you're new to these conver
 sations or actively engaged in public life\, this discussion offers a wel
 coming space to learn from one another\, share perspectives\, and conside
 r how informed civic participation can create positive change.\nJoin us f
 or:\n\nA screening of the award-winning documentary All In: The Fight for
  Democracy\nA facilitated discussion on the film's relevance to today's p
 olitical climate\nMeaningful conversation with fellow students\, faculty\
 , and staff\nFree food and refreshments\nCivic-themed giveaways\nResource
 s to help you stay informed and engaged\n\nThis event is open to all stud
 ents\, faculty\, and staff. Come for the film\, stay for the conversation
 \, and leave with a deeper understanding of the importance of civic parti
 cipation and the power of every voice.\nGood film. Great conversation. Fr
 ee food. Giveaways. One important conversation about the future of our de
 mocracy.\n\nHosted by: Civic & Voter Engagement\n\nAdditional Information
  can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12540192
DTEND:20261014T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050250Z
DTSTART:20261014T150000Z
LOCATION:Cohen Lounge-Dickson Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:All In: The Fight for Democracy Film Screening & Civic Engagement 
 Experience
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12540192
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12540192
X-HOSTS:Civic & Voter Engagement
END:VEVENT
