CATEGORIES:Large Scale
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking about applying to law school? Join us for our
  44th Annual NJ Law School Day at Montclair State University! All NJ coll
 ege students and alumni who are interested in applying to law school are 
 welcome to attend!\nAt NJ Law School Day\, you can speak with law school 
 representatives from NJ\, NY\, and across the U.S. about what their progr
 ams have to offer and how you can prepare to be a strong law school candi
 date.  Whether you are new to the idea of applying to law school or prepa
 ring to apply this fall\, this event is a great opportunity to learn and 
 connect.\n\n \nWhat to Expect from Law School Day:\n1pm - 2pm - Law Schoo
 l Panel Discussion\n- For this session\, you will hear from a panel of la
 w school representatives about what they look for when reviewing law scho
 ol applications and how to become a strong law school candidate.\n \n2 - 
 4pm - The Law School Fair\n- This is your chance to meet face-to- face wi
 th law school representatives from NJ\, NY\, PA\, MA and across the U.S.\
 , and ask questions about applying to law school!\n- The list of law scho
 ols attending is growing! Current law schools attending include: American
 \, Fordham\, Villanova\, Ohio State\, Seton Hall\, Rutgers\, Drexel\, Pen
 n State\, Pace\, Syracuse\, Cardozo\, Utah\, Maryland\, West Virginia\, R
 ichmond\, Pittsburgh\, and many\, many more.  \n- You can see the full li
 st of law schools attending once you RSVP on Handshake on or after Septem
 ber 1\, 2026\n \n3:30 - 4:30 PM - Speed Mentoring: Pathways to Public Ser
 vice\n- After learning what it takes to get into law school\, stick aroun
 d to connect directly with professionals who are doing the work.  \n- Thr
 ough fast-paced\, small-group rotating conversations\, you’ll discover re
 al-world career paths\, and get honest insights into public interest and 
 public service work. Come listen\, ask questions\, grab a snack\, and mak
 e connections that can kickstart your legal\, public interest\, or public
  service career.\n \nHow to Be Prepared for Law School Day:\n\nBe ready t
 o share information about you\, your interests\, and your goals!\nWrite d
 own the questions you have about law schools and the process of applying 
 to law school\nBring something to take notes\nDress to impress!  Business
  attire is recommended\nRegistration for Law School Day will open on Sept
 ember 1\, 2026 on Handshake\nQuestions? Need law school advice? Email Chr
 ysten Colacicco\, Pre-Law Program Coordinator at MSU\, at colaciccoc@mont
 clair.edu\n\n\n\nHosted by: College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CH
 SS)\, Civic & Voter Engagement\, Government Relations and Community Affai
 rs \, Pre-Law Society\, Pre-Law Program\n\nAdditional Information can be 
 found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12564033
