DESCRIPTION:Are you pursuing a career that requires a graduate or professi
 onal degree? Do you need help planning your next steps after graduation?\
 nJoin us for the Graduate and Health Professions School Fair to meet admi
 ssion representatives from both graduate and health profession schools! T
 he Pre-Medical Program and The Office for Experiential Education and Care
 er Connections invite students of all levels and majors to connect with a
 dmissions representatives in a wide variety of fields! Students can also 
 attend professional development and admission preparation workshops durin
 g the fair.\nMore Information:\n \n\nFree to attend for all Montclair and
  Bloomfield campus students and alums.\nCome prepared with questions to a
 sk each school representative.\nBring plenty of copies of your resume.\nW
 orkshops on professional development and tips for the admissions process 
 will be offered during the fair.\nStudents must bring their Montclair Sta
 te University Student IDs.\nRegistration is required through Handshake.\n
 Students who attend will receive giveaways.\nProfessional attire is highl
 y encouraged.\nThe proceeds from this fair allow the Pre-Medical Program 
 to provide free admissions test preparation resources to our pre-med and 
 pre-health students!\n\nEvent details:\n\nGraduation and Health Professio
 ns School Fair\n\nLocation: University Hall\, 7th Floor (Conference Cente
 r)\nTime: 12 PM - 3 PM\n\n\n\n\nGraduate School-focused workshop(s): \n\n
 Psyched for Grad School: 1:40 PM - 3:30 PM in University Hall Room 1020 (
 RSVP Here)\n\n\n\n \n\nHosted by: Pre-Medical Program\n\nAdditional Infor
 mation can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/127
 64597
